#, xml-text
msgid "Config Files"
msgstr ""

#.  ~/.nailrc seems not to be supported anymore
#.         <filename>
#. /etc/nail.rc</filename>, <filename>~/.mailrc</filename>
#.         and <filename>~/.nailrc</filename>
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:172
#, xml-text
msgid "<filename>/etc/nail.rc</filename> and <filename>~/.mailrc</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:176
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/nail.rc"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:180
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.mailrc"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:190
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:193
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For displaying mails, <application>mailx</application> uses a pager program."
" Since the default of <command>pg</command> is not available on a LFS "
"system, its required to specify which pager is to use. By default, there is "
"<command>more</command> and the more comfortable <command>less</command> "
"installed. If the variable PAGER is not set in "
"<filename>/etc/profile</filename> or <filename>~/.bash_profile</filename>, "
"or if it should be another pager just for reading mails, it can be set "
"system wide in <filename>/etc/nail.rc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:205
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:207
#, xml-text
msgid "or individually for the actual user in <filename>~/.mailrc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:209
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set PAGER=<replaceable>&lt;more|less&gt;</replaceable>\" "
"&gt;&gt; ~/.mailrc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:212
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Other interesting options to set in the config files might be EDITOR and "
"MAILDIR."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:217
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If not set in the environment for other packages, the default editor can be "
"set by:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:221
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo \"set "
"EDITOR=<replaceable>&lt;vim|nano|...&gt;</replaceable>\" &gt;&gt; "
"/etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:224
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Depending on which kind of <xref linkend=\"server-mail\"/> is installed, it "
"might be required to set the MAILDIR variable so "
"<application>mailx</application> is able to find the mails:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/networking/mailnews/mailx.xml:229
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>echo \"set MAILDIR=Maildir\" &gt;&gt; /etc/nail.rc</userinput>"
msgstr ""

